# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

## [0.4.0] - 2026-01-10

### Added
- Service request system for ordering additional services during stay
  - New `service_requests` table in database
  - `ServiceRequest` model and `ServiceRequestRepository` for persistence
  - Service costs integration into checkout process
- Checkout summary endpoint (`GET /api/checkouts/summary/<booking_id>`) displaying booking price and service costs
- Multiple bookings display in check-in/check-out workflow
  - When searching by guest name, all eligible bookings are shown for selection
  - Improved UX for handling guests with multiple room bookings
- Cash payment option in payment page alongside wallet payment
- Cancel booking modal with reason input and deposit loss warning
- CSS extraction for better maintainability
  - Extracted inline CSS from `contact.html` to `css/contact.css`
  - Extracted inline CSS from `my-bookings.html` to `css/my-bookings.css`
- Dashboard improvements for checked-in users
  - "Phòng Đang Sử Dụng" section displaying only checked-in rooms
  - Service ordering functionality directly from dashboard
  - View ordered services modal with total price updates
- Automatic room assignment during check-in (no manual room ID input required)
- Room status auto-update: rooms are set to 'reserved' when booking is created, 'available' when cancelled
- Smooth scroll navigation from homepage menu to sections (GIỚI THIỆU, PHÒNG)
- Room listing UI redesign with modern card layout matching provided design

### Changed
- Booking flow refactored: redirects to `payment.html` before creating booking
  - Booking details saved as draft in `localStorage`
  - Actual booking creation happens after payment confirmation or cash selection
- Check-in process: automatic room assignment based on room type
  - Removed requirement for manual room ID input
  - System automatically selects available room matching booking's room type
- Check-out process: displays service costs and calculates total amount
  - Shows breakdown of booking price, service costs, and total payment
  - Service requests are included in checkout calculation
- Dashboard: removed booking statistics, focused on current stay management
  - Only displays checked-in rooms for active users
  - Total price dynamically updates when services are ordered
- Receptionist panel: enhanced check-in/check-out search
  - Displays all matching bookings when multiple rooms are booked
  - Improved selection interface for choosing which booking to process
- Room detail page: added validation to prevent booking unavailable rooms
  - Disables booking button for 'occupied', 'maintenance', or 'reserved' rooms
- Payment service: removed automatic booking confirmation after payment
  - Bookings remain 'pending' until manually confirmed by receptionist
- Booking service: improved error handling with rollback on payment failure
  - Booking is cancelled if payment processing fails
  - Room status is reverted if booking creation fails

### Fixed
- Fixed booking status incorrectly showing 'confirmed' immediately after creation
  - Bookings now correctly remain 'pending' until receptionist confirmation
- Fixed room status not updating to 'reserved' when booking is created
  - Rooms are now properly reserved upon successful booking
- Fixed wallet balance validation: users cannot proceed with booking if insufficient funds
- Fixed check-in foreign key constraint error for `receptionist_id`
  - System gracefully handles invalid receptionist IDs by setting to NULL
- Fixed checked-in rooms not displaying in dashboard
  - Corrected JavaScript destructuring of `checkoutSummary` in room data
- Fixed room availability validation in `room-detail.html`
  - Prevents booking attempts for unavailable rooms
- Fixed TabError (inconsistent tabs/spaces) in `checkin_service.py`
- Fixed requirements.txt security vulnerabilities
  - Updated Flask to 3.1.2
  - Updated flask-cors to 6.0.0
  - Updated mysql-connector-python to 9.5.0
  - Updated python-dotenv to 1.2.1

### Security
- Updated dependencies to latest versions to address security vulnerabilities

## [0.3.0] - 2026-01-02

### Added
- Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) system with middleware decorators
  - `require_auth` - Requires user authentication
  - `require_admin` - Requires administrator role
  - `require_receptionist_or_admin` - Requires receptionist or administrator role
  - `require_role` - Custom role-based access
  - `optional_auth` - Optional authentication
- Admin access restrictions - Admins cannot access user booking pages
- User role-based redirects after login/registration
- Frontend authentication middleware with automatic header injection
- Admin panel access control and navigation restrictions

### Changed
- Updated all API routes with appropriate authentication/authorization decorators
- Frontend API calls now automatically include `X-User-Id` header
- Login/registration redirects users based on their role (admin → admin.html, user → dashboard.html)
- Navigation menus adapt based on user role

### Fixed
- Admin users can no longer access user-specific pages (dashboard, booking, my-bookings, payment)
- Proper error handling for 401 (Unauthorized) and 403 (Forbidden) responses
- Session management improvements

## [0.2.0] - 2025-12-31

### Added
- MySQL database integration replacing in-memory storage
  - Database configuration module (`db_config.py`) with environment variable support
  - Connection pooling and error handling
  - Migration from in-memory dictionaries to MySQL tables
- Environment variable configuration (`.env` file) for database credentials
- Database schema implementation with all tables:
  - users, staff, rooms, bookings, payments, services, coupons, checkins, checkouts, reports
- Repository layer refactored for MySQL:
  - All CRUD operations now use MySQL queries
  - Transaction management with rollback support
  - Proper data type conversions and null handling
- Database connection testing script

### Changed
- All repository classes migrated from in-memory storage to MySQL
- Data persistence across application restarts
- Improved error handling for database operations

### Security
- Database credentials moved to environment variables (`.env` file)
- Connection strings no longer hardcoded in source code

## [0.1.0] - 2025-12-06

### Added
- Initial project setup
- Project structure with layered architecture (Models, Views, Controllers, Services, Repositories)
- Flask backend API with RESTful endpoints
- Frontend UI with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript
- Basic authentication system (login/registration)
- Room management functionality
- Booking system
- Payment processing
- Service management
- Staff management
- Report generation
- README.md
- Changelog

### Added - Core Features
- User registration and login
- Room CRUD operations
- Booking creation and management
- Payment processing
- Service catalog
- Staff management
- Report generation
- Dashboard for users
- Admin panel for administrators

### Added - Frontend Pages
- Homepage (index.html)
- Login page (login.html)
- Registration page (register.html)
- Dashboard (dashboard.html)
- Booking page (booking.html)
- My Bookings (my-bookings.html)
- Admin Panel (admin.html)
- Payment page (payment.html)

### Added - Backend Architecture
- Models: User, Room, Booking, Payment, Service, Staff, Coupon, CheckIn, Report
- Controllers: UserController, RoomController, BookingController, PaymentController, etc.
- Services: Business logic layer for all entities
- Repositories: Data access layer (initially in-memory, later migrated to MySQL)
- Views: Response formatting layer
